	"en": [
		{"key": "home", "title": "Demiurges wiki", "category": "wiki", "html": "<h1>Demiurges wiki</h1><p>An encyclopedia of <strong>Etherlords</strong> (2001) and <strong>Etherlords II</strong> (2003): every creature, sorcery, enchantment, artifact, hero skill and specialization of both games, with its statistics, description and picture, and what Etherlords II changed. It belongs to <strong>Demiurges</strong>, a fan-made engine that plays both games from your own copy.</p><h2>Encyclopedia</h2><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>Section</th><th>Contents</th></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://all-creatures\">Creatures</a></td><td>Every creature by race: ether cost, power, toughness and abilities</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://all-spells\">Sorceries and enchantments</a></td><td>Every spell by race: type, rarity and ether cost</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://all-artifacts\">Artifacts</a></td><td>Artifacts, including those that summon a creature</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://all-skills\">Hero skills</a></td><td>Skills and the effect of each rank</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://all-specializations\">Specializations</a></td><td>Chance-based talents of heroes</td></tr></table><p>A card has one page for both games. Its table shows the two editions side by side: a highlighted value is one Etherlords II changed, and a card that only one game has says so. The lists mark each entry with the games that have it (I, II).</p><p>Open a creature's page in the game to rotate and zoom its 3D model. Choose an action below the model and press <strong>Play</strong> to preview attacks, hit reactions, and deaths with their original sounds when available. See <a href=\"wiki://creatures\">About creatures</a> for the controls.</p><h2>Game mechanics</h2><ul><li><a href=\"wiki://races\">The four races</a> · <a href=\"wiki://combat\">How a battle works</a> · <a href=\"wiki://combat-phases\">Turn and phases</a> · <a href=\"wiki://attack-defence\">Attack and defence</a></li><li><a href=\"wiki://abilities\">Creature abilities</a> · <a href=\"wiki://automatic-combat\">Automatic combat and the camera</a> · <a href=\"wiki://adventure-map\">The adventure map</a></li><li><a href=\"wiki://creatures\">About creatures</a> · <a href=\"wiki://spells\">About spells</a> · <a href=\"wiki://runes-artifacts\">Runes and artifacts</a> · <a href=\"wiki://heroes\">Heroes and levels</a></li></ul><h2>Story and world</h2><ul><li><a href=\"wiki://story-world\">The world of ether</a> · <a href=\"wiki://story-peoples\">Races and peoples</a> · <a href=\"wiki://places\">Places</a> · <a href=\"wiki://story-characters\">Characters</a></li><li><a href=\"wiki://chaots\">Chaots</a> · <a href=\"wiki://kinets\">Kinets</a> · <a href=\"wiki://vitals\">Vitals</a> · <a href=\"wiki://synthets\">Synthets</a> · <a href=\"wiki://pale\">The Pale</a></li><li><a href=\"wiki://diamanda\">Diamanda</a> · <a href=\"wiki://white-lord\">The White Lord</a></li><li><a href=\"wiki://story-el1\">The story of Etherlords</a> · <a href=\"wiki://story-el2\">The story of Etherlords II</a></li></ul><h2>Campaigns and modes</h2><ul><li><a href=\"wiki://campaign-el1\">Etherlords campaigns</a> · <a href=\"wiki://campaign-el2\">Etherlords II campaigns</a> · <a href=\"wiki://duel\">Duel</a></li></ul><h2>Playing on Demiurges</h2><p class=\"note\">Demiurges contains no game content. You need your own copy of the game you want to play. The GOG editions are the tested ones.</p><ul><li><a href=\"wiki://installing\">Installing the game files</a> · <a href=\"wiki://browser\">Playing in the browser</a> · <a href=\"wiki://main-menu\">Main menu, saves and settings</a> · <a href=\"wiki://controls\">Controls</a> · <a href=\"wiki://options\">Options</a></li><li><a href=\"wiki://differences\">Differences from the originals</a> · <a href=\"wiki://troubleshooting\">Problems and reporting</a> · <a href=\"wiki://about-wiki\">About this wiki</a></li></ul>", "search": "demiurges wiki an encyclopedia of etherlords (2001) and etherlords ii (2003): 